.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
is a structure which holds a set of ASN.1 conversion, printing and
information methods for a specific public key algorithm.
.Pp
There are two places where the
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
objects are stored: one is a built-in array representing the standard
methods for different algorithms, and the other one is a stack of
user-defined application-specific methods, which can be manipulated by
using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_asn1_add0 3 .
.Ss Methods
The methods are the underlying implementations of a particular public
key algorithm present by the
.Vt EVP_PKEY
object.
.Bd -literal
 int (*pub_decode) (EVP_PKEY *pk, const X509_PUBKEY *pub);
 int (*pub_encode) (X509_PUBKEY *pub, const EVP_PKEY *pk);
 int (*pub_cmp) (const EVP_PKEY *a, const EVP_PKEY *b);
 int (*pub_print) (BIO *out, const EVP_PKEY *pkey, int indent,
                   ASN1_PCTX *pctx);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr pub_decode 3
and
.Xr pub_encode 3
methods are called to decode / encode
.Sy X509_PUBKEY
ASN.1 parameters to / from
.Fa pk .
They MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
They're called by
.Xr X509_PUBKEY_get0 3
and
.Xr X509_PUBKEY_set 3 .
.Pp
The
.Xr pub_cmp 3
method is called when two public keys are to be compared.
It MUST return 1 when the keys are equal, 0 otherwise.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_eq 3 .
.Pp
The
.Xr pub_print 3
method is called to print a public key in humanly readable text to
.Fa out ,
indented
.Fa indent
spaces.
It MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_print_public 3 .
.Bd -literal
 int (*priv_decode) (EVP_PKEY *pk, const PKCS8_PRIV_KEY_INFO *p8inf);
 int (*priv_encode) (PKCS8_PRIV_KEY_INFO *p8, const EVP_PKEY *pk);
 int (*priv_print) (BIO *out, const EVP_PKEY *pkey, int indent,
                    ASN1_PCTX *pctx);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr priv_decode 3
and
.Xr priv_encode 3
methods are called to decode / encode
.Sy PKCS8_PRIV_KEY_INFO
form private key to / from
.Fa pk .
They MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
They're called by
.Xr EVP_PKCS82PKEY 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY2PKCS8 3 .
.Pp
The
.Xr priv_print 3
method is called to print a private key in humanly readable text to
.Fa out ,
indented
.Fa indent
spaces.
It MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_print_private 3 .
.Bd -literal
 int (*pkey_size) (const EVP_PKEY *pk);
 int (*pkey_bits) (const EVP_PKEY *pk);
 int (*pkey_security_bits) (const EVP_PKEY *pk);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr pkey_size 3
method returns the key size in bytes.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_size 3 .
.Pp
The
.Xr pkey_bits 3
method returns the key size in bits.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_bits 3 .
.Bd -literal
 int (*param_decode) (EVP_PKEY *pkey,
                      const unsigned char **pder, int derlen);
 int (*param_encode) (const EVP_PKEY *pkey, unsigned char **pder);
 int (*param_missing) (const EVP_PKEY *pk);
 int (*param_copy) (EVP_PKEY *to, const EVP_PKEY *from);
 int (*param_cmp) (const EVP_PKEY *a, const EVP_PKEY *b);
 int (*param_print) (BIO *out, const EVP_PKEY *pkey, int indent,
                     ASN1_PCTX *pctx);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr param_decode 3
and
.Xr param_encode 3
methods are called to decode / encode DER formatted parameters to / from
.Fa pk .
They MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
They're called by
.Xr PEM_read_bio_Parameters 3
and the
.Sy file:
.Xr OSSL_STORE_LOADER 3 .
.Pp
The
.Xr param_missing 3
method returns 0 if a key parameter is missing, otherwise 1. It's called
by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_missing_parameters 3 .
.Pp
The
.Xr param_copy 3
method copies key parameters from
.Fa from
to
.Fa to .
It MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_copy_parameters 3 .
.Pp
The
.Xr param_cmp 3
method compares the parameters of keys
.Fa a
and
.Sy b .
It MUST return 1 when the keys are equal, 0 when not equal, or a
negative number on error.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_parameters_eq 3 .
.Pp
The
.Xr param_print 3
method prints the private key parameters in humanly readable text to
.Fa out ,
indented
.Fa indent
spaces.
It MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_print_params 3 .
.Bd -literal
 int (*sig_print) (BIO *out,
                   const X509_ALGOR *sigalg, const ASN1_STRING *sig,
                   int indent, ASN1_PCTX *pctx);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr sig_print 3
method prints a signature in humanly readable text to
.Fa out ,
indented
.Fa indent
spaces.
.Sy sigalg
contains the exact signature algorithm.
If the signature in
.Fa sig
doesn't correspond to what this method expects,
.Xr X509_signature_dump 3
must be used as a last resort.
It MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
It's called by
.Xr X509_signature_print 3 .
.Bd -literal
 void (*pkey_free) (EVP_PKEY *pkey);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr pkey_free 3
method helps freeing the internals of
.Fa pkey .
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_free 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_set_type 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_set_type_str 3 ,
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_assign 3 .
.Bd -literal
 int (*pkey_ctrl) (EVP_PKEY *pkey, int op, long arg1, void *arg2);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr pkey_ctrl 3
method adds extra algorithm specific control.
It's called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_default_digest_nid 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_set1_encoded_public_key 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get1_encoded_public_key 3 ,
.Xr PKCS7_SIGNER_INFO_set 3 ,
.Xr PKCS7_RECIP_INFO_set 3 ,
\&...
.Bd -literal
 int (*old_priv_decode) (EVP_PKEY *pkey,
                         const unsigned char **pder, int derlen);
 int (*old_priv_encode) (const EVP_PKEY *pkey, unsigned char **pder);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr old_priv_decode 3
and
.Xr old_priv_encode 3
methods decode / encode they private key
.Fa pkey
from / to a DER formatted array.
These are exclusively used to help decoding / encoding older (pre
PKCS#8) PEM formatted encrypted private keys.
.Xr old_priv_decode 3
MUST return 0 on error, 1 on success.
.Xr old_priv_encode 3
MUST the return same kind of values as
.Xr i2d_PrivateKey 3 .
They're called by
.Xr d2i_PrivateKey 3
and
.Xr i2d_PrivateKey 3 .
.Bd -literal
 int (*item_verify) (EVP_MD_CTX *ctx, const ASN1_ITEM *it, void *asn,
                     X509_ALGOR *a, ASN1_BIT_STRING *sig, EVP_PKEY *pkey);
 int (*item_sign) (EVP_MD_CTX *ctx, const ASN1_ITEM *it, void *asn,
                   X509_ALGOR *alg1, X509_ALGOR *alg2,
                   ASN1_BIT_STRING *sig);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr item_sign 3
and
.Xr item_verify 3
methods make it possible to have algorithm specific signatures and
verification of them.
.Pp
.Xr item_sign 3
MUST return one of:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It <=0
error
.It 1
.Xr item_sign 3
did everything, OpenSSL internals just needs to pass the signature
length back.
.It 2
.Xr item_sign 3
did nothing, OpenSSL internal standard routines are expected to continue
with the default signature production.
.It 3
.Xr item_sign 3
set the algorithm identifier
.Sy algor1
and
.Sy algor2 ,
OpenSSL internals should just sign using those algorithms.
.El
.Pp
.Xr item_verify 3
MUST return one of:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It <=0
error
.It 1
.Xr item_sign 3
did everything, OpenSSL internals just needs to pass the signature
length back.
.It 2
.Xr item_sign 3
did nothing, OpenSSL internal standard routines are expected to continue
with the default signature production.
.El
.Pp
.Xr item_verify 3
and
.Xr item_sign 3
are called by
.Xr ASN1_item_verify 3
and
.Xr ASN1_item_sign 3 ,
and by extension,
.Xr X509_verify 3 ,
.Xr X509_REQ_verify 3 ,
.Xr X509_sign 3 ,
.Xr X509_REQ_sign 3 ,
\&...
.Bd -literal
 int (*siginf_set) (X509_SIG_INFO *siginf, const X509_ALGOR *alg,
                    const ASN1_STRING *sig);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr siginf_set 3
method is used to set custom
.Sy X509_SIG_INFO
parameters.
It MUST return 0 on error, or 1 on success.
It's called as part of
.Xr X509_check_purpose 3 ,
.Xr X509_check_ca 3
and
.Xr X509_check_issued 3 .
.Bd -literal
 int (*pkey_check) (const EVP_PKEY *pk);
 int (*pkey_public_check) (const EVP_PKEY *pk);
 int (*pkey_param_check) (const EVP_PKEY *pk);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr pkey_check 3 ,
.Xr pkey_public_check 3
and
.Xr pkey_param_check 3
methods are used to check the validity of
.Fa pk
for key-pair, public component and parameters, respectively.
They MUST return 0 for an invalid key, or 1 for a valid key.
They are called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_check 3 ,
.Xr EVP_PKEY_public_check 3
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_param_check 3
respectively.
.Bd -literal
 int (*set_priv_key) (EVP_PKEY *pk, const unsigned char *priv, size_t len);
 int (*set_pub_key) (EVP_PKEY *pk, const unsigned char *pub, size_t len);
.Ed
.Pp
The
.Xr set_priv_key 3
and
.Xr set_pub_key 3
methods are used to set the raw private and public key data for an
EVP_PKEY. They MUST return 0 on error, or 1 on success.
They are called by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_new_raw_private_key 3 ,
and
.Xr EVP_PKEY_new_raw_public_key 3
respectively.
.Bd -literal
 size_t (*dirty) (const EVP_PKEY *pk);
 void *(*export_to) (const EVP_PKEY *pk, EVP_KEYMGMT *keymgmt);
.Ed
.Pp
.Xr dirty_cnt 3
returns the internal key's dirty count.
This can be used to synchronise different copies of the same keys.
.Pp
The
.Xr export_to 3
method exports the key material from the given key to a provider,
through the
.Xr EVP_KEYMGMT 3
interface, if that provider supports importing key material.
.Ss Functions
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_new
creates and returns a new
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
object, and associates the given
.Fa id ,
.Fa flags ,
.Fa pem_str
and
.Fa info .
.Fa id
is a NID,
.Fa pem_str
is the PEM type string,
.Fa info
is a descriptive string.
The following
.Fa flags
are supported:
.Bd -literal
 ASN1_PKEY_SIGPARAM_NULL
.Ed
.Pp
If
.Sy ASN1_PKEY_SIGPARAM_NULL
is set, then the signature algorithm parameters are given the type
.Sy V_ASN1_NULL
by default, otherwise they will be given the type
.Sy V_ASN1_UNDEF
(i.e.
the parameter is omitted).
See
.Xr X509_ALGOR_set0 3
for more information.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_copy
copies an
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
object from
.Fa src
to
.Fa dst .
This function is not thread safe, it's recommended to only use this when
initializing the application.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_free
frees an existing
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
pointed by
.Fa ameth .
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_add0
adds
.Fa ameth
to the user defined stack of methods unless another
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
with the same NID is already there.
This function is not thread safe, it's recommended to only use this when
initializing the application.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_add_alias
creates an alias with the NID
.Fa to
for the
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
with NID
.Fa from
unless another
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
with the same NID is already added.
This function is not thread safe, it's recommended to only use this when
initializing the application.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_public ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_private ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_param ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_free ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_ctrl ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_item ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_siginf ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_check ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_public_check ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_param_check ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_security_bits ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_set_priv_key ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_set_pub_key ,
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_get_priv_key
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_get_pub_key
set the diverse methods of the given
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
object.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get0_asn1
finds the
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
associated with the key
.Fa pkey .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_new
returns NULL on error, or a pointer to an
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
object otherwise.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_add0
and
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_add_alias
return 0 on error, or 1 on success.
.Pp
.Fn EVP_PKEY_get0_asn1
returns NULL on error, or a pointer to a constant
.Vt EVP_PKEY_ASN1_METHOD
object otherwise.
.Sh HISTORY
The signature of the
.Em pub_decode
functional argument of
.Fn EVP_PKEY_asn1_set_public
has changed in OpenSSL 3.0 so its
.Fa pub
parameter is now constified.
